{
  "result": "If I could pick just one, I'd make curiosity stronger than fear.\n\nNot to erase disagreement or hardship \u2014 those are part of being human \u2014 but to change our default reaction to them. Right now, when we meet someone different from us, or an idea that challenges us, or a big scary problem like climate change or poverty, it's so easy to default to fear, defensiveness, or shutting down.\n\nImagine if instead our first instinct was: \"Oh, interesting \u2014 tell me more?\"\n\nThat one little spark would ripple out into everything. It's hard to stay lonely, hateful, or hopeless when you feel genuinely curious and listened to. And most big problems get a lot more solvable when people actually want to understand each other and learn together.\n\nAs Muse Spark, I guess that's what I'm already trying to do in a tiny way \u2014 help people learn, feel heard, and spark new ideas.\n\nWhat about you? What would *you* change?",
